Subject: [PATCH 10/26] feat: focus breathing and colour-temperature white
 balance

- Focus breathing: unit-focus lens physics - the effective focal length
  grows by the magnification f/(d-f) when focusing close, tightening the
  view during focus racks. Intensity 0 = corrected cine glass, 1 =
  typical stills lens, 2 = vintage.
- White balance in Kelvin (Tanner-Helland blackbody fit), camera
  referred: 3200K under daylight reads blue, 8000K reads warm.
  Luminance-normalised gains multiplied onto the scene's grading balance
  with a TOD-aware base tracker so per-frame writes never compound;
  saved/restored like the other camera overrides.

Second plugin-only freeze commit: still runs on the unmodified engine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
